<title>FRANCE: Rouen grain exports jumped to 605,150 T in April.</title>
<headline>Rouen grain exports jumped to 605,150 T in April.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exports from Rouen jumped to 605,150 tonnes in April 1997 from 373,000 tonnes in April 1996, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The April 1997 grain total included 458,195 tonnes of wheat, 145,350 tonnes of barley and 1,605 tonnes of maize.</p>
<p>Officials gave the following breakdown by destination (in tonnes).</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    South Africa		  14,500</p>
<p>    West Africa		   41,200</p>
<p>    Algeria			 23,519</p>
<p>    Canary Islands		14,700</p>
<p>    Cuba			    36,131</p>
<p>    Egypt			   61,500</p>
<p>    Britain			 16,027</p>
<p>    Greece			   5,775</p>
<p>    Italy			  178,683</p>
<p>    Morocco			 11,400</p>
<p>    Tunisia			 23,260</p>
<p>    Turkey			  31,500</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Saudi Arabia		  88,167</p>
<p>    Cyprus			  25,158</p>
<p>    Greece			   2,750</p>
<p>    Tunisia			 29,275</p>
<p>MAIZE</p>
<p>    Britain			  1,605</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
